Third-party data in this repository
-----------------------------------

The files below are, or are built from, third-party data, under the
licence shown. data/manifests/<id>.json gives each source's licence,
where it was read, its attribution and what it is used for; the packs'
manifest.json "credits" credit the sources of each pack.

- Wikipedia, Wikisource, Wikiquote and Wikibooks text, by their
  contributors. CC BY-SA 4.0. Built into the packs' lexicons and models
  and the English lexicons (apps/ios/KeyboardExtension/Lexicon/*.fst);
  sampled sentences in the next-word eval sets (data/eval/next-ml.heldout.txt,
  next-ml.tune.txt, next-en.tune.txt, and the next-*.heldout.txt and
  next-*.tune.txt files in data/eval/as, hi and ta, with the synthetic
  romanised sets data/eval/as/next-romanised*.tsv made from them); short
  quoted spans in data/eval/**/memorisation.json.
  Manifests: data/manifests/*wiki*.json.
- English Wikinews, by Wikinews contributors. CC BY 2.5 and CC BY 4.0.
  Language model training text (the ml and hi packs); sentences in
  data/eval/next-en.tune.txt. data/manifests/enwikinews.json.
- Project Gutenberg texts. Public domain. Language model training text
  (the ml and hi packs). data/manifests/gutenberg.json.
- Dakshina dataset v1.0, Google Research (Roark et al., 2020). CC BY-SA
  4.0. Transliterator training data for the packs that credit it; the
  eval extracts data/eval/translit-human.tsv, hi/translit-human.tsv,
  si/translit-human.tsv, next-manglish*.tsv, hi/next-hinglish*.tsv and
  ta/next-tanglish*.tsv. data/manifests/dakshina.json.
- Aksharantar, AI4Bharat (Madhani et al., 2022). Manually collected data
  CC BY; mined data and existing sources CC0 1.0; includes Wikidata
  labels (CC0). Transliterator training data and romanisation tables for
  the packs that credit it; the eval extracts
  data/eval/<id>/translit-human.tsv (manual rows, CC BY) for as, bho, bn,
  gu, kn, mai, mr, ne, or, pa, ta, te and ur.
  data/manifests/aksharantar*.json.
- SMC Malayalam Speech Corpus, conversation sentences, Swathanthra
  Malayalam Computing. CC BY-SA 4.0. data/eval/next-ml.txt.
  data/manifests/smc-msc-conversations.json.
- SMC Malayalam word lists, Swathanthra Malayalam Computing. CC BY-SA
  3.0. Built into packs/ml.neopack/ml.fst. data/manifests/smc-words.json.
- Unicode CLDR emoji annotations and Unicode Emoji data (emoji-test.txt),
  Copyright (c) 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc. Unicode License v3, full notice
  in LICENSES/Unicode-3.0.txt. The emoji-words.txt and emoji-search.txt
  files in data/langs/, packs/ and apps/ios/KeyboardExtension/Emoji/, and
  apps/ios/KeyboardExtension/Emoji/emoji.txt.
  data/manifests/cldr-annotations.json, unicode-emoji.json.
- SCOWL (Spell Checker Oriented Word Lists) 2020.12.07. Used to choose
  the words of the English lexicon (apps/ios/KeyboardExtension/Lexicon/
  en.fst). data/manifests/scowl.json. Its notice:
    Copyright 2000-2018 by Kevin Atkinson. Permission to use, copy,
